From 20a561c90c23877366fa80da72e51918d86f0a26 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ji Mao Cai <44921326+jinghero@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:11:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] windows: allocate and recover owned temporary VM files on
 demand

Initialize ownership tracking only when creating a temporary hardware INI,
cache pair or read-only drive overlay. Ordinary drive queries do not pin
directories or scan receipts. Bind later allocations to the original
launch paths and retain the session across runtime share-mode changes.

Reserve private files with read-data pins in the resolved TEMP directory.
Keep user-sealed receipts in the owning AVD and validate directory, leaf
and file identities before deletion. Preserve legacy and unproven files.
Write private INIs in place, reserve both cache files, and keep backing
paths within the Windows block layer byte limit.

Retain existing non-Windows and permanent-drive error behavior. Report
failed Windows temporary allocations through their existing callers.
---
